## What is this?

An **Expo React Native** application scaffolded from the `apps/mobile/react-native` boilerplate template. It targets **iOS**, **Android**, and **Web** from a single TypeScript codebase using:

- **Expo SDK 57** (React Native 0.86, React 19.2)
- **Expo Router** — file-based routing with typed routes
- **Tamagui** — universal UI components that compile to `<View>` on native and `<div>` on web
- **Solito** — cross-platform navigation (unifies Expo Router and Next.js Router)
- **TypeScript** — strict mode, typed routes, shared types with the monorepo

## Sharing code with web

This app shares code with the Next.js web app (`apps/active/web/`) through shared workspace packages:

- `@{{ monorepo_name }}/ui` — Tamagui design system (universal components)
- `@{{ monorepo_name }}/app` — shared screens and feature modules (via Solito)
- `@{{ monorepo_name }}/api` — typed API client and zod schemas
- `@{{ monorepo_name }}/config` — shared env, theme tokens, constants

Both apps import the same packages via `workspace:*`.

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 22.13+ (per Expo SDK 57)
- pnpm 9.5+
- Expo CLI (via `npx expo`)

### Development

```bash
# From the monorepo root
pnpm install

# Start the Expo dev server (iOS/Android/Web)
pnpm nx start {{ package_name }}

# Start for a specific platform
pnpm nx dev {{ package_name }}          # dev client
npx expo start --ios                     # iOS simulator
npx expo start --android                 # Android emulator
npx expo start --web                     # Web browser
```

### Building

```bash
# Export for all platforms
pnpm nx build {{ package_name }}

# Export for a specific platform
pnpm nx build:ios {{ package_name }}
pnpm nx build:android {{ package_name }}
pnpm nx build:web {{ package_name }}

# Prebuild native projects (generates ios/ and android/ directories)
pnpm nx prebuild {{ package_name }}
```

### EAS Build & Update

```bash
# Configure EAS (first time only)
npx eas-cli init

# Build for stores
pnpm nx eas-build {{ package_name }}

# Push an OTA update
pnpm nx eas-update {{ package_name }}
```

### Testing & Quality

```bash
pnpm nx test {{ package_name }}         # Run tests (Vitest)
pnpm nx lint {{ package_name }}          # Lint (ESLint)
pnpm nx typecheck {{ package_name }}     # Type check (tsc --noEmit)
```

## Project Structure

```
{{ package_name }}/
├── app/                    # Expo Router file-based routes
│   ├── _layout.tsx         # Root layout (Tamagui + SafeArea + GestureHandler providers)
│   ├── index.tsx           # Home screen
│   └── about.tsx           # About screen
├── assets/                 # App icons and splash screen images
├── src/                    # App-specific (non-shared) code
├── app.json                # Expo configuration
├── eas.json                # EAS Build profiles
├── babel.config.js         # Babel config (Tamagui + Reanimated)
├── metro.config.js         # Metro bundler config (Tamagui plugin)
├── tamagui.config.ts       # Tamagui theme/token configuration
├── tsconfig.json           # TypeScript config
├── project.json            # Nx project config (targets: start/dev/build/test/lint)
└── package.json            # Dependencies (workspace:* for shared packages)
```

## AI Agent Setup

This project is compatible with AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex). When you run `npx create-expo-app`, Expo scaffolds `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` files — this template follows the same convention. See the [Expo AI agents documentation](https://docs.expo.dev/agents) for setup instructions.

## Technologies

- **Framework**: Expo SDK 57 (React Native 0.86)
- **Routing**: Expo Router (file-based, typed routes)
- **UI**: Tamagui (universal design system)
- **Navigation**: Solito (cross-platform)
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict)
- **Build**: Nx (monorepo orchestration)
- **Testing**: Vitest
- **Linting**: ESLint + Prettier
- **EAS**: Expo Application Services (Build + Update)
